---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Ornament from '../components/Ornament.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Why The Tipsy Goose is exploring a more personal, capable, and honest alternative to meal kit delivery.">
  <header class="page-masthead"><div class="shell relative z-10 py-14 lg:py-20"><p class="eyebrow text-brass-bright">About the project</p><h1 class="mt-7 max-w-5xl font-display text-[clamp(3.2rem,7vw,6.3rem)] leading-[.9] tracking-[-.04em]">Dinner deserves better than autopilot.</h1></div></header>
  <div class="shell grid gap-14 py-16 lg:grid-cols-[.7fr_1.3fr] lg:py-24">
    <aside class="lg:sticky lg:top-8 lg:self-start"><p class="eyebrow">The short version</p><Ornament class="mt-5 text-brass" compact /><p class="mt-7 font-display text-4xl leading-[1.08]">Use the machine for range. Use the kitchen for truth.</p></aside>
    <article class="prose max-w-3xl">
      <p>The Tipsy Goose is a home cooking and cocktail publication built around a simple suspicion: the planning convenience of a meal kit does not require the box.</p>
      <p>Generative AI can help turn a peculiar set of constraints—what you like, what is in the refrigerator, how much time is left, which cuisine you are curious about—into a useful starting point. Ordinary grocery stores supply the ingredients. Human creativity sets the direction. Cooking supplies the evidence.</p>
      <h2>Ideas are not recipes yet.</h2>
      <p>We draw a bright line between something proposed and something cooked. Every recipe has an editorial status: <strong>draft</strong>, <strong>experimental</strong>, or <strong>kitchen-tested</strong>. When AI contributed, the recipe can say how. When cooking changed the idea, that belongs in the record too.</p>
      <h2>The whole evening counts.</h2>
      <p>A good dinner is not merely a main dish. It is timing, a useful technique, the right drink, and enough breathing room to enjoy the people at the table. That is why this publication includes coordinated menus and kitchen notes alongside recipes.</p>
      <h2>What this page does not claim.</h2>
      <p>This is a project statement, not an invented founder story. The prelaunch site does not imply a catalog that does not exist, publish fictional ratings, or pass untested development examples off as dinner. The archive will grow at the pace of actual editorial work.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
